  "query_preview": "..Tuesday and Wednesday look dry and cool as high pressure \nslides across. By Thanksgiving, amplified troughing over the mid CONUS\nis showing up with differences on how close a surface low could be to \nWisconsin. Also looks marginally cold enough for some snow over the \narea. Details are uncertain and ensembles are not in agreement, so \nthere remains some questions for sure. Pops are slowly increasing for \nthis time frame, so it bears watching. Stay tuned!    \n\nTemperatures...Say so long to highs in the 60s. Cold front brings steady \nor slowly falling temperatures Sunday, but many areas will still reach \n50 degrees into the afternoon. Temperatures finally drop a bit below\nnormal Monday and Tuesday, with highs in the 30s. Slight moderation\nto near normal temps Wednesday and Thanksgiving, with slightly \nabove normal after that into next weekend.",
